host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan swell -- a long-standing quarrel reads where the outcome is read
prompt Keaton set the autonomous loop running: pick up the thread from the newest log recommend, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first under the Microkernel Target double-seat, close reds first, prove on metal, send often.
think Opened as Kyri -- context/KYRI.md and context/RADIANT_STYLE.md read before anything else, then crux/REMEMBER.md, the 1024-round itinerary, the eight-season double-seat, and the Rye-first crypto wave.
think Standfast first: crux/REDS.md reads every living row CLOSED -- %96 and %97 both closed on 20260820.030440 with witnesses on metal. No open agent-closable red, so constructive work may begin.
think Running thread: the newest three log rows are Caravan rungs -- endure, heed, relent, dwell -- and dwell's recommend names the next door plainly: nothing in the arc lets a plan treat a quarrel of two runs differently from one of two hundred, so the honest next rung is whether a long-standing position earns a louder place in the record.
think Council rota, lap index 73 mod 27 = 19 -- context/KYRI.md, deep-read at the lap open as the voice preamble; read context/QUIN.md beside it so the rota supplement was genuinely a second reading rather than a restatement of the preamble.
think Named the rung under the Comlink tendency -- clear, fun, safe. swell greps clean across the tree as an identifier; the only hits are ordinary English in Lotus prose and one counsel line, so nothing seated collides.
think Found a real collision inside the module instead: the arc already owns a type named Standing, from the repose rung. Renamed the new reading to Volume with quiet and loud, rather than shadowing a word seventy rungs deep.
think Built the rung the way the arc builds every rung -- swell.rye accretes over dwell.rye, wrapping its Report as inner, delegating every fold below to dwelling_rung, and adding one tier to each named accessor.
think Two build faults caught the shape honestly: run_of ends in .run rather than .inner so the accessor bump missed it, and date_the_standing still wrote aged/undated/ageless into this rung's own Report when those fields now live one tier down. Both repointed rather than papered over.
think The design decisions each earned their prose. The threshold is a module constant no run may pass in, because a bound a plan could choose would let any plan quiet its oldest quarrel by naming a larger number -- a supervisor grading the objections raised against itself.
think The reading comes off the wire rather than off memory: the run opens the age actually written beside the position, and SwellUndated refuses by name where no age is there at all, since a standing computed from an age nobody wrote would read loudest of all.
think Ordered the heralding last of all, after the dating, because the age this rung reads is the age that dating just left on the wire -- and the relenting at the top of the run may already have taken down the very position a standing would speak about.
think Proved five RED paths on metal before claiming anything. SwellMisrecorded by skipping the write with the read-back armed. SwellEarly by disarming both endings and the honest fold, which catches it before the run can. SwellUndated by argument alone -- .untold beside .heralded -- which is what makes that guard load-bearing. SwellMiscounted by counting one position as both published and unpublished.
think The planted control is the finding itself: every guard disarmed at once and the selftest prints GREEN while caravan/.swells/plan.swell does not exist and plan.standing still reads p beside an age of 4. An operator would open a quarrel four runs old and be told its standing was published.
think Turned the long-function ratchet my own rung raised -- run_in_swell reached 71 lines, so the call-site comment tightened to one line with the reasoning kept in the callee's doc. The tree-wide past-70 roster is clean again.
obs The measurement is deliberately narrow, and that narrowness is the honest part. A quarrel raised on this very run is fairly read at its own volume and costs the count nothing; only the long-standing position an operator reads no louder than a fresh one moves the number.
obs A herald reports and never argues. Both runs settle carried out whole, leave the quarrel exactly where its holder left it, leave the age untouched at 4, and keep the word standing under it. This rung says how loudly a position reads and nothing else.
obs The standing falls with the quarrel and survives a provisioning, exactly as the age does -- a byte left behind beside the outcome would go on shouting for a quarrel its own holder let go.
obs SwellUndated is reachable by argument with no code change at all, which is a stronger proof than a planted probe: the guard stands on a configuration the module genuinely admits.
loom witness=caravan_swell_witness rungs=73 selftest_wall_ms=428 module_lines=9200 witness_lines=263 red_paths=5
loom caravan=suite_choir witnesses=73 verdict=GREEN cold_tree=yes
file caravan/swell.rye the rung -- a long-standing quarrel published where the outcome is read, four refusals by name
file tools/caravan_swell_witness.rish the witness on metal, reading every claim natively per the apostrophe loom
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers the new rung so the choir sings 73 in one voice
file caravan/README.md the durable per-rung record this card no longer has to carry
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge refreshed; the dwell chronicle condensed to a pointer
file session-logs/README.md the newest-first index row
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, makes the inheriting run answer for it, lets its holder close it, says how long a standing one has stood, and finally reads that age aloud where an operator opens the outcome -- so the question above is what a plan owes a quarrel it has now published as long-standing: the record says loud and nothing in the arc asks the plan to do anything differently about it, which means a supervisor may announce an old objection forever and still run exactly as it always ran.
